      "message": "Andy, I know this fix is a bit speculative, but I don\u0027t have a full understanding at this moment. Initially I added rounding to powers of 2 to bring the remote submix buffer size to 1024 as it was on HIDL. The test which was failing uses 8 kHz SR and 688 frame count which w/o this fix gets rounded up to 1024. For 8 kHz that\u0027s a big difference. I\u0027m still not sure why the test was failing because according to AF dumps and Perfetto, reads do work in both cases, however the change of timing from ~80ms to ~120ms makes this test to fail—this is something about behavior of MediaCodec which is used when recording audio from camera.",
